    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0183" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2216</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moser</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-17T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1918,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 3, 3 p.m., somewhat garbled. As emergency measure and without
                    commitment to permanent support Red Cross authorizes you to draw up to $5,000.
                    Meanwhile please report: (1) Organization <pb facs="0184" n="134" xml:id="pg134"
                    /> and competence of personnel Harbin Red Cross Chapter; (2) any additional
                    funds urgent now; (3) probable requirements both material and financial for
                    30,000 refugees in Manchuria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
